IMPORT prelude

-- Copyright Act 2021 (Singapore) -- how long copyright lasts in authorial works and sound recordings (ss 114, 122), contracting out of
-- permitted uses (ss 186 to 188), fair use (ss 190 to 192), the deemed fair use for research or study and the "reasonable portion"
-- (ss 43, 194), and computational data analysis (s 244).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CA2021.txt (amendments to
-- Act 31 of 2022).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 13 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to duration and the user-side permitted
-- uses. Not encoded: subsistence and ownership, the exclusive rights, infringement, remedies, the other permitted uses (education,
-- libraries, disability and so on), moral rights, performers' rights, rights management, and collective licensing.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Copyright Act 2021 -- uses`

§§ `114, 122 -- duration`

-- s 114(1): an authorial work first published within 50 years of being made: copyright expires (a) 70 years after the end of the
-- year the author dies, if the author is identified within 70 years of publication; (b) otherwise 70 years after the end of the year
-- of first publication. (3): an unpublished work -- 70 years after death, or 70 years after it was made if the author is not
-- identified.
-- s 122(1)(a): a sound recording published within 50 years of being made -- 70 years after the end of the year of first publication.
-- The function gives the LAST YEAR of protection: copyright "expires 70 years after the end of the year", so the work is free from
-- 1 January of the following year.
GIVEN `author identified` IS A BOOLEAN, `year of death` IS A NUMBER, `year of first publication` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last year of copyright in a published work` MEANS
    IF `author identified` THEN `year of death` PLUS 70 ELSE `year of first publication` PLUS 70

GIVEN `year of first publication` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last year of copyright in a sound recording` MEANS
    `year of first publication` PLUS 70

§§ `186 to 188 -- contracting out`

-- s 186(1), (2): a rights owner may exclude or restrict a permitted use by contract ONLY if the contract is "individually negotiated"
-- AND the term is "fair and reasonable" (judged by bargaining strength, inducements, notice, and whether the contract works without
-- it).
-- s 187(1): a term is VOID so far as it excludes or restricts a permitted use for public collections (libraries and archives, except
-- s 234), computer programs, COMPUTATIONAL DATA ANALYSIS, or judicial proceedings and legal advice.
-- s 188: a foreign choice-of-law clause that excludes a permitted use is void if imposed mainly to evade it, or against a Singapore
-- consumer contracting in Singapore.
--
-- A standard-form website licence cannot take away fair use (it is not individually negotiated), and no contract at all can take
-- away the computational data analysis exception.
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `fair use`
    `computational data analysis`
    `computer program backup`
    `library copying`
    `use in legal proceedings`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use, `individually negotiated` IS A BOOLEAN, `fair and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a contract term can exclude the use` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `fair use` THEN `individually negotiated` AND `fair and reasonable`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `190 to 192 -- fair use`

-- s 190: fair use of a work is a permitted use. s 191: all relevant matters, including (a) purpose and character, commercial or
-- non-profit educational; (b) the nature of the work; (c) amount and substantiality; (d) effect on the market. (These are weighed by
-- a court; the encoding takes the conclusion as an input.)
-- s 192(1): use for REPORTING NEWS is not fair unless sufficiently acknowledged, or acknowledgment is impractical. (2): use for
-- CRITICISM OR REVIEW is not fair unless sufficiently acknowledged -- no impracticality exception.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `reporting news`
    `criticism or review`
    `other`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `fair on the factors` IS A BOOLEAN, `acknowledged` IS A BOOLEAN, `acknowledgment impractical` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is fair` IF
        `fair on the factors`
    AND CONSIDER `the purpose`
        WHEN `reporting news` THEN `acknowledged` OR `acknowledgment impractical`
        WHEN `criticism or review` THEN `acknowledged`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `43, 194 -- copying for research or study`

-- s 194(1): copying a literary, dramatic or musical work for research or study is DEEMED fair (s 191 not applied) if it is an article
-- in a periodical or no more than a "reasonable portion" is copied. (2): not two articles from the same issue on different subjects.
-- s 43(1)(a): for an edition of 10 or more pages, a reasonable portion is 10% or less of the pages, OR pages all from the SAME CHAPTER.
GIVEN `pages in the edition` IS A NUMBER, `pages copied` IS A NUMBER, `all from one chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the copy is a reasonable portion` IF
        `pages in the edition` AT LEAST 10
    AND (`pages copied` TIMES 10 AT MOST `pages in the edition` OR `all from one chapter`)

§§ `244 -- computational data analysis`

-- s 244: copying for computational data analysis is a permitted use if the copy is used for nothing else, is supplied only to verify
-- results or for collaborative research, and X has LAWFUL ACCESS to the source. Illustrations: circumventing a PAYWALL is not lawful
-- access; breaching a database's terms of use is not lawful access (ignoring terms void under s 187). And the source must not be an
-- infringing copy, unless X did not know (and, for a flagrantly infringing site, could not reasonably have known).
DECLARE Source HAS
    `used only for the analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `circumvented a paywall` IS A BOOLEAN
    `breached valid terms of use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the source was infringing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or should have known it was infringing` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the source` IS A Source
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the copying is permitted for data analysis` IF
        `the source`'s `used only for the analysis`
    AND (NOT `the source`'s `circumvented a paywall`)
    AND (NOT `the source`'s `breached valid terms of use`)
    AND ((NOT `the source`'s `the source was infringing`) OR (NOT `the source`'s `knew or should have known it was infringing`))
